  ;; ---- corpus source datasets (ADR-2608041800) ---------------------------
  ;; Only the index/ layer of these is consumed. raw/ is git-annex content
  ;; living in Backblaze B2 and is NOT fetched by this repository or by its
  ;; CI: a projection must be rebuildable without downloading 2.46 GB of
  ;; statutory text.
  ;;
  ;; :source/ci-checkout false on all four, and this is a REAL GAP, not a
  ;; design choice. .github/workflows/contract.yml needs four more
  ;; actions/checkout steps and two more run steps (bin/build-corpus.cljs and
  ;; test/corpus_contract.clj) -- the exact YAML is in docs/ci-design.md. The
  ;; agent that landed this change could not push it: the OAuth token in use
  ;; lacks GitHub's `workflow` scope, which blocks both `git push` of a
  ;; workflow file and the Contents API (the latter answers 404 rather than
  ;; 403). Until someone with that scope applies it, CI rebuilds and gates the
  ;; CATALOG only, and data/corpus/** is committed output that CI does not
  ;; independently reproduce. bin/verify-ci-lock.cljs prints this loudly on
  ;; every run rather than letting it pass silently.
